# KNOWN GAP — 🚨 A CoW COLLECTION ALIAS LOSES ITS SEMANTICS INSIDE A LOOP,
# in BOTH directions. Silent wrong values at rc 0; ASan-clean.
#
# Straight-line, the CoW value semantics of a second name for a collection
# are CORRECT and are pinned by `cow_transitive_alias.gg`:
#
#     Vector[String] alias = v ; alias.push("b")   ->  v=1  alias=2   ✓
#     Vector[String] alias = v ; v.push("b")       ->  v=2  alias=1   ✓
#
# Put the SAME mutation inside a `while` loop and both directions break:
#
#   A. MUTATION THROUGH THE ALIAS — every push is LOST.
#      3x `alias.push` in a loop leaves `alias.len() == 1`.
#   B. MUTATION THROUGH THE ROOT — the alias is never SEVERED, so value
#      semantics silently degrades to REFERENCE semantics: both names report
#      the grown length.
#
# INTENDED (asserted by the #[ignore]d test citing this file):
#     alias-loop 1 4
#     root-loop 4 1
# MEASURED at HEAD, Rust gg, C and LLVM alike:
#     alias-loop 1 1        <- A: three pushes vanished
#     root-loop 4 4         <- B: the alias was never severed
#
# ⊕ THE SELF-HOST LANE IS CORRECT ON BOTH. Run through
# `self_host_lowerer/driver.gg --emit-c` it prints the INTENDED output above,
# so the oracle adjudicates this and Rust gg is the lagging lane.
#
# NOT the `known_gaps/cow_loop_bare_param_*` family: every member of that
# family is about a bare (borrow) PARAM or `self`, and that is enforced
# mechanically — both the loop and scope pre-header hooks filter their
# candidate set with `ctx.is_bare_param` (`src/ir/lowering/stmts/mod.rs:2632`
# and `:2699`). A LOCAL collection alias is not a bare param, so it is
# outside the candidate set of the whole 2G machinery and no fix there
# reaches it. Their symptom also differs: that family throws away a private
# copy per iteration (wrong counts, extra clones); this one loses appends
# outright and turns value semantics into reference semantics.
#
# NOT the alias-SPELLING UAF class either (`cow_alias_spelled_*`): that one
# is a dangling STRING VIEW into the collection — rc 139, ASan
# heap-use-after-free, realloc load-bearing. This is rc 0, ASan-clean,
# realloc-independent (3 iterations), and the wrong thing is the collection
# alias's own length.

void main():
    Vector[String] a = []
    a.push("a")
    Vector[String] a_alias = a
    int i = 0
    while i < 3:
        a_alias.push("b")
        i = i + 1
    print(f"alias-loop {a.len()} {a_alias.len()}")

    Vector[String] b = []
    b.push("a")
    Vector[String] b_alias = b
    int j = 0
    while j < 3:
        b.push("b")
        j = j + 1
    print(f"root-loop {b.len()} {b_alias.len()}")
